WEBVTT

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:02.563
Now we move to one of the most useful tools in this

00:00:02.589 --> 00:00:08.357
module the case expression Think of case as a
sequence of questions

00:00:09.273 --> 00:00:14.247
SQL checks the first WHEN condition If it is TRUE
SQL returns

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:18.951
the corresponding THEN value and stops If it is not
true SQL

00:00:18.977 --> 00:00:23.062
moves to the next WHEN condition If none of the
conditions match

00:00:23.255 --> 00:00:27.984
SQL uses ELSE If there is no ELSE the result becomes
null

00:00:29.726 --> 00:00:34.637
The most important phrase to remember is first match
wins That means

00:00:34.663 --> 00:00:39.134
the order of the branches matters Whenever you build
a case expression

00:00:39.418 --> 00:00:42.485
read the conditions from top to bottom and ask
whether an earlier

00:00:42.511 --> 00:00:46.248
condition could accidentally capture records that
were supposed to reach a later

00:00:46.261 --> 00:00:46.815
condition
